Embracing the DevSecOps Paradigm
Learning Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

• Understand the core principles of DevSecOps and its importance in modern software development • Integrate security scanning tools (SonarQube, Dependency Check, ZAP) into CI/CD pipelines • Implement secret management using HashiCorp Vault • Create and validate Infrastructure as Code (IaC) templates using Terraform • Integrate Open Policy Agent (OPA) for policy enforcement • Design application architecture and perform threat modeling using Microsoft Threat Modeling Tool • Build a comprehensive DevSecOps pipeline from scratch

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

• Basic understanding of software development lifecycle • Familiarity with Linux command line operations • Basic knowledge of Git version control • Understanding of containerization concepts (Docker) • Basic networking concepts • Familiarity with YAML and JSON formats

